/*  debugToggleT -- `debug ALL X` MARKS X'S SUBTREE AND RUNNING IT AGAIN UNDOES IT.

    Tony's shape: `debug X` TOGGLES `debugged` on X, and GroupItem::setDebug propagates the
    toggle down -- every component whose state does not already agree with X's NEW state flips
    and recurses. The subtree ends up agreeing with the root, so the same command run twice walks
    it straight back. Tony's reason, in his words: "so I can run DEBUG twice with the same
    parameters to undo what the first run does."

    ⚠ THIS FIXTURE EXISTS BECAUSE THE QUESTION WAS UNASKABLE UNTIL 2026-09-18. `debugged` has no
    reader anywhere in the tree -- its consumers were directive-injected and culled by C-155 --
    so on a bare build `debug ALL X` is INVISIBLE, and the only thing the fleet could have said
    about it is that nothing complained. The `debuggeD` GroupFields accessor was minted to make
    it readable, read-only and with the DEBUG rule as its single writer, and this is what it was
    minted for. Its predecessor `debugAllT` asserted a count that the toggle design does not
    produce and was deleted rather than re-pinned.

    THE ROWS, and each one is doing separate work.
      IV-0  everything reads 0 before anything runs. The baseline, and the row that stops IV-1
            passing against a flag that was already set.
      IV-1  ⚠ DEPTH BY NAME, NOT BY COUNT. top, mid and leaf all read 1 after one command. A
            walk that stopped at depth 1 would read top=1 mid=0 leaf=0 and a count-based check
            could not tell that from a smaller tree.
      IV-1  ⚠ AND `outside` IS THE NEGATIVE CONTROL AND IS NOT OPTIONAL. dbgOut is a sibling
            rule that is NOT under dbgTop, and it must stay 0 -- otherwise 1/1/1 is equally
            satisfied by a mechanism that simply marks every rule it can reach.
      IV-2  the involution: the same command again, and every value is back to 0. Without the
            toggle this row reads 1/1/1 and the feature is a one-way trip.  */
Start();
register(Grokking);
define
    dbgLeaf     "leafA" "leafB";
    dbgMid      dbgLeaf "midX";
    dbgTop      dbgMid "topY";
    dbgOut      "outsideA" "outsideB";
    ;
search Grokking list;

cerr "IV-0 before      top=" dbgTop.debuggeD " mid=" dbgMid.debuggeD " leaf=" dbgLeaf.debuggeD " outside=" dbgOut.debuggeD:;
debug ALL dbgTop;
cerr "IV-1 after one   top=" dbgTop.debuggeD " mid=" dbgMid.debuggeD " leaf=" dbgLeaf.debuggeD " outside=" dbgOut.debuggeD:;
debug ALL dbgTop;
cerr "IV-2 after two   top=" dbgTop.debuggeD " mid=" dbgMid.debuggeD " leaf=" dbgLeaf.debuggeD " outside=" dbgOut.debuggeD:;

print "DEBUGTOGGLET SENTINEL -- reached the foot":;
stop();
